{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: H-bridge and single-phase inverter",
  "exampleId": "block-inverters",
  "description": "The H-bridge switches its two legs in opposition, so its output averages (2D − 1) · 24 V = 12 V at D = 0.75: 6 A through 2 Ω once the 10 mH inductance has settled. The inverter leg switches between +12 V and −12 V; its duty cycle follows 0.5 + 0.4 sin(2π·50t), so its output averages a 9.6 V, 50 Hz sine. Over a positive half-cycle that averages 2/π of 9.6 V.",
  "duration": 0.05,
  "revision": 0,
